␀еЌЦЅ!„еЌЅЁб…BMX1␀BIOS bank extension descriptor missing or does not match ABI 1.0.␀Banked SRAM unavailable: INFO %04x, status %u.
␀Install matching firmware and CP/M system image, then restart.␀<1 ms (below timer resolution)␀%lu ms; %lu.%lu KiB/s␀FAIL: banked write rejected.␀FAIL: millisecond stopwatch read after write.␀FAIL: banked read rejected.␀FAIL: millisecond stopwatch read after read.␀FAIL: verification at offset %u, expected %02x, got %02x
␀FAIL: local RAM write stopwatch read.␀FAIL: local RAM write verification at offset %u
␀FAIL: local RAM read stopwatch read.␀FAIL: local RAM read verification at offset %u
␀Bulk: base RAM 2 x 2048-byte copies; banked RAM 1 x 4096-byte call.␀256-byte chunks: 16 calls per direction for both memory types.␀%lu KiB per timed direction (%u repeats); local copies use runtime memcpy.
␀Direction | Z80 base RAM | Banked RAM␀Write     | ␀ | ␀Read      | ␀PASS: banked payload and both local RAM copy directions verified after timing.␀FAIL: banked SRAM unavailable; check BIOS, firmware and A16 wiring.␀FAIL: need a contiguous 4096-byte allocation; %u bytes free.
␀FAIL: allocation cleanup or heap free-size check.␀MEMPERF: Z80 base RAM versus banked SRAM, repeated 4 KiB workload.␀BANKMEM API: one 4 KiB call, then 16 x 256-byte calls.␀4 KiB base buffer; preparation, poisoning and verification excluded.␀Base RAM uses two 2 KiB buffer regions; neither code nor CP/M is overwritten.␀Timing: port 0x17, stopwatch 0, whole milliseconds; no output while timing.␀32 repeats move 128 KiB per direction to reduce 1 ms rounding noise.␀PASS: MEMPERF complete; %u bytes free.
