␀BANK 1␀Bank 1␀upper("Bank 1") = "%s".
␀Read 128 bytes from A:AUTORUN.COM in bank 1; byte sum %u.
␀Export %s: %s
␀ADD16␀void()␀BLKFREE␀state:i8@8␀BANKDATA␀Read a 128-byte slice of a 4096-byte bank-owned block.␀PASS: flat record in/out/inout, 32-bit values, arrays and guards.␀DATA.LIB␀FAIL: library cleanup.␀DATATEST: ordinary C calls, separate banks.␀[1/8] Load DATA.LIB and run onload␀PASS: load and lifecycle.␀[2/8] Integer arguments and results␀PASS: scalar values and 16-bit wraparound.␀[3/8] Counted text buffer (inout)␀PASS: text copy-back, limits and null-pointer rejection.␀[4/8] File I/O in bank 1 (out)␀PASS: file read, reopen and buffer guards.␀[5/8] Export discovery and rejected calls␀PASS: eight exports, signatures and malformed-frame rejection.␀[6/8] Flat records, bank-owned blocks and opaque handles␀PASS: chunk data, bounds, stale handles and double-free rejection.␀[7/8] Unload and check shared runtime state␀PASS: directory search preserved and transfer memory recovered.␀[8/8] Reload, reject old handles, clean up an open block, reset the pool␀PASS: reload isolation, unload cleanup and pool-reset rejection.␀PASS: all 8 bank-1 library checks.␀FAIL: step %u (transport error %u).
